# Architecture Guidelines

## Repository Pattern

Data access must go through a repository class. Controllers and services must never query the database directly.

```
Controller → Service → Repository → Database
```

```typescript
// BAD — querying DB directly in a service
async getUser(id: number) {
  return this.db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1', [id]);
}

// GOOD — delegating to a repository
async getUser(id: number): Promise<IUser> {
  return this.userRepository.findById(id);
}
```

Repositories live in a `repositories/` folder alongside their domain (e.g. `server_1/src/repositories/`).

## Business Logic in Service Layers

Keep all business logic inside service classes. Controllers only handle HTTP concerns (parsing request, returning response).

```typescript
// BAD — business logic in controller
async createOrder(req: Request, res: Response) {
  if (req.body.items.length === 0) throw new Error('Empty order');
  const total = req.body.items.reduce((sum, i) => sum + i.price, 0);
  await this.orderRepo.save({ ...req.body, total });
  res.json({ success: true });
}

// GOOD — controller delegates to service
async createOrder(req: Request, res: Response) {
  const order = await this.orderService.createOrder(req.body);
  res.json(order);
}
```

Services live in a `services/` folder (e.g. `server_1/src/services/`).
